after molecule-based selection. Thus, improved biomarkers are required. In this study, we use an image analysis to capture morphologic attributes relating to the spatial interaction and architecture of tumor cells and tumor-infiltrating lymphocytes (TILs) from digitized H&E images. We evaluate the association of image features with progression-free (PFS) and overall survival in non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) (<i>N</i> = 187) and gynecological cancer (<i>N</i> = 39) patients treated with ICIs. We demonstrated that the classifier trained with NSCLC alone was associated with PFS in independent NSCLC cohorts and also in gynecological cancer. The classifier was also associated with clinical outcome independent of clinical factors. Moreover, the classifier was associated with PFS even with low PD-L1 expression. These findings suggest that image analysis can be used to predict clinical end points in patients receiving ICI.", "affiliation": "Center for Computational Imaging and Personalized Diagnostics, Case Western Reserve University, Cleveland, OH, USA.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print-Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["research-article", "Journal Article"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "U01 CA248226", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "U54 CA254566", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIBIB NIH HHS", "acronym": "EB", "grantId": "R43 EB028736", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "R01 CA208236", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "R01 CA216579", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "R01 CA220581", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "U24 CA199374", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "R01 CA202752", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "U01 CA239055", 